@* Marks a region as read-only. Does two things:
   1. Cascades GupReadOnly, which the GUP field components honour natively
      (real disabled/readonly attributes, so keyboard and screen readers agree).
   2. Blocks pointer interaction on the region itself, which catches bespoke
      markup a page hand-rolls outside the component library.
   The cascade is the real fix; the pointer block is the safety net. *@

<CascadingValue Value="ReadOnly" Name="GupReadOnly">
    @if (ReadOnly)
    {
        <div class="gup-readonly-region" aria-disabled="true" style="pointer-events:none;">
            @ChildContent
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        @ChildContent
    }
</CascadingValue>

@code {
    [Parameter] public bool ReadOnly { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
